        <article class="min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-16 pb-24 text-[15px] leading-7 text-gray-700">

            <header>
                <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Documentation</p>
                <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900">How Windcraft works</h1>
                <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-gray-600">The gallery, projects, the editor and agents, step by step. If a word looks unfamiliar, check the <a href="#glossary" class="font-medium text-gray-900 underline">glossary</a> at the bottom.</p>
            </header>

            <section id="what" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">What is Windcraft?</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">Windcraft has two doors. The <strong class="text-gray-900">gallery</strong> is where you come to look at designs and choose one. The <strong class="text-gray-900">editor</strong> is where you make a design, with its code beside it. Every design lives in a <strong class="text-gray-900">project</strong>.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">It is for developers who want code to copy, designers who want to work visually, teams who want one look across a product, and anyone building with an AI coding tool. It is free.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="start" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Quick start</h2>
                <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Open the <a href="/" class="font-medium underline">gallery</a>, pick a category, and look at a design. Press <em>Code</em> to see it, and the copy button to take it. No account needed.</li><li>Press <strong class="text-gray-900">Open in editor</strong> to make your own copy, or <strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong> to keep it. Both ask which project it goes in.</li><li>Or press <strong class="text-gray-900">New design</strong> in the top bar: a dialog opens with the code on the left and the design on the right. Write or paste code, press Save, and choose its project. (On the Projects page the top bar has <strong class="text-gray-900">New project</strong>, which makes a project and opens the editor on a blank page with the code panel below it.)</li><li>Set the project's look (colours, font, corners) on its page, then turn <strong class="text-gray-900">Public</strong> on for any design you want to share in the gallery.</li></ol>
            </section>

            <section id="gallery" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">The gallery</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">The gallery is organised by category.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Preview and Code</strong>: switch between how a design looks and its code. Pick a phone size, light or dark, or full screen.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Copy</strong>: copy the code. You need no account for this.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong>: put a private copy into one of your projects.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Open in editor</strong>: make your own copy in a project and open it.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="projects" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Projects</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">A project is where everything starts: a design cannot exist outside one. It is a folder for your pages and components, with one shared look, a share link, and a place to export from.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">New project</strong> (top bar) creates it at once and opens the editor on a blank page. Rename it on its page.</li><li>The project page shows a board of every page and component. Drag frames to arrange them. Two tabs list them as <strong class="text-gray-900">Pages</strong> and <strong class="text-gray-900">Components</strong>: a design's category decides which (the Pages category group are pages, every other category is a component).</li><li>Select an item to <strong class="text-gray-900">export</strong> it, see its <strong class="text-gray-900">history</strong> and restore a version, <strong class="text-gray-900">move</strong> it to another project, say whether AI may use it as a <strong class="text-gray-900">reference</strong>, or <strong class="text-gray-900">delete</strong> it.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Import</strong> adds designs from HTML files, a zip, or pasted HTML. Long pages can be split into sections.</li><li>Deleting a project deletes everything in it.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="editor" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">The editor</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">The editor shows the design and its code side by side. Edit either: change the code and the design follows, drag or restyle on the canvas and the code follows.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Tools</strong>: select, hand, interact (try the page as it will run), frame, shapes, text, and an add menu.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Code panel</strong>: syntax colours, auto-closing tags, find and replace, Tailwind class suggestions, and <strong class="text-gray-900">Format</strong> to tidy it. It sits below the design by default; the dock button moves it to the left, and your choice is remembered.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Properties</strong>: edit an element's spacing, size, type, colour, border and effects. Each value is written to where it comes from (a Tailwind class or CSS).</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong> asks only for a name the first time.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="theme" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">A project's look</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">On the project page, the <strong class="text-gray-900">Theme</strong> tab holds four choices that the editor, every preview and your exports use:</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Brand colour</strong>: one colour. Its eleven shades become <code>brand-50</code> to <code>brand-950</code>, and the colour itself is <code>brand-600</code>.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Gray</strong>: which of Tailwind's five grays <code>gray-*</code> means here.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Font</strong>: a Google Fonts family, or the system font.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Corners</strong>: how round <code>rounded-*</code> is.</li></ul>
                <p class="mt-3">Change it once and every page and component in the project follows.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="share" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Publishing and sharing</h2>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Public</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">Designs are private. Turn <strong class="text-gray-900">Public</strong> on for a design on its project page and it appears in the gallery, under its category, where anyone can look at it and copy the code.</p>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Share link</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">The <strong class="text-gray-900">Share</strong> button on a project page makes a link. Anyone who opens it can look at the whole project in its theme and copy the code, with no account. Nothing in it can be changed. <strong class="text-gray-900">Stop sharing</strong> ends the link.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="export" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Export and history</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">Any design can be copied or exported as HTML, React, Vue or Svelte, and as a design spec or a profile. The page code stays plain HTML with Tailwind, so you are never locked in.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">To keep the project's look in exported code, take the theme setup too: it is a small Tailwind config for the brand colour, gray, font and corners.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">Every change keeps the earlier version. Open an item's <em>History</em> to see them and restore one.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="agents" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Coding agents (MCP)</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">MCP lets Claude Code, Cursor and similar tools read and write your projects, instead of guessing.</p>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Set it up (once)</h3>
                <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Open <a href="/connect" class="font-medium underline">Connect</a> in the sidebar.</li><li>Press <em>Generate token</em> and copy the command now. The token is shown once.</li><li>Paste the command into your terminal. For Claude Code it looks like this:</li></ol>
                <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 font-mono text-[12px] leading-5 text-gray-900">claude mcp add --transport http tailwind-library https://YOUR-SITE/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN"</pre>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What the agent can do</h3>
                <div class="mt-3 divide-y divide-gray-200 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white text-sm"><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_design_guide</code><span>A summary of your designs: colours, fonts, spacing and an index. Agents read it first.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">search_components</code><span>Find designs by keyword or tag.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_component</code><span>Get one design as HTML, React, Vue or Svelte.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_design_spec</code><span>Look at a design as a labelled tree of elements.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">apply_design_patch</code><span>Make small changes to a design by element id.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">save_component, save_design, save_pages</code><span>Save a component, a finished page, or several pages. Every save goes into a project: name one, or set an active project.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">list_tags</code><span>List your tags.</span></div></div>
                <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-gray-900">Treat the token like a password.</strong> Anyone who has it can read and add to your projects. If it leaks, generate a new one.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="glossary" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Glossary</h2>
                <dl class="mt-4 divide-y divide-gray-200 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white text-sm"><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Gallery</dt><dd>Public designs, by category, most liked first.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Project</dt><dd>Where designs live: a folder with a shared look, a share link and exports.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Page and component</dt><dd>A page is a whole screen; a component is a smaller part. Both live in a project.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Theme</dt><dd>A project's brand colour, gray, font and corners.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Public</dt><dd>A design turned on for the gallery. Private by default.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Share link</dt><dd>A view-only link to a whole project.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">MCP</dt><dd>The standard that lets coding tools use your projects.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Token</dt><dd>A secret that proves a tool may use your projects.</dd></div></dl>
                <p class="mt-6 text-sm">Still stuck? See <a href="/support" class="font-medium underline">Support</a>.</p>
            </section>

        </article>
    </div>
</main>

<script>
    (function () {
        var links = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#toc .toc-link'));
        var sections = links.map(function (a) { return document.getElementById(a.getAttribute('href').slice(1)); });

        function update() {
            var current = 0;
            var atBottom = window.innerHeight + window.scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 4;
            if (atBottom) {
                current = sections.length - 1;
            } else {
                sections.forEach(function (sec, i) {
                    if (sec && sec.getBoundingClientRect().top <= 140) current = i;
                });
            }
            links.forEach(function (a, i) { a.classList.toggle('is-active', i === current); });
        }

        window.addEventListener('scroll', update, { passive: true });
        window.addEventListener('resize', update);
        update();
    })();
</script>
